Determine the {@link Bitmap.CompressFormat} given the {@link ImageFormat}. If no match is
found, it returns {@link Bitmap.CompressFormat#JPEG}

@param format The {@link ImageFormat} used as input
@return The corresponding {@link Bitmap.CompressFormat}

code:
private static Bitmap.CompressFormat getOutputFormat(@Nullable final ImageFormat format) {
    if (format == null) {
      return Bitmap.CompressFormat.JPEG;
    }

    if (format == DefaultImageFormats.JPEG) {
      return Bitmap.CompressFormat.JPEG;
    } else if (format == DefaultImageFormats.PNG) {
      return Bitmap.CompressFormat.PNG;
    } else {
      if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= Build.VERSION_CODES.ICE_CREAM_SANDWICH
          && DefaultImageFormats.isStaticWebpFormat(format)) {
        return Bitmap.CompressFormat.WEBP;
      }

      return Bitmap.CompressFormat.JPEG;
    }
  }

public Map<CharSequence, Set<Cookie>> getCachedCookies() {
		if (!STATE.compareAndSet(this, NOT_READ, READING)) {
			for (; ; ) {
				if (state == READ) {
					return cachedCookies;
				}
			}
		}

		List<String> allCookieHeaders = nettyHeaders.getAll(cookiesHeaderName);
		Map<String, Set<Cookie>> cookies = new HashMap<>();
		for (String aCookieHeader : allCookieHeaders) {
			Set<Cookie> decode;
			if (isClientChannel) {
				final Cookie c = ((ClientCookieDecoder) decoder).decode(aCookieHeader);
				Set<Cookie> existingCookiesOfName = cookies.get(c.name());
				if (null == existingCookiesOfName) {
					existingCookiesOfName = new HashSet<>();
					cookies.put(c.name(), existingCookiesOfName);
				}
				existingCookiesOfName.add(c);
			}
			else {
				decode = ((ServerCookieDecoder) decoder).decode(aCookieHeader);
				for (Cookie cookie : decode) {
					Set<Cookie> existingCookiesOfName = cookies.get(cookie.name());
					if (null == existingCookiesOfName) {
						existingCookiesOfName = new HashSet<>();
						cookies.put(cookie.name(), existingCookiesOfName);
					}
					existingCookiesOfName.add(cookie);
				}
			}
		}
		cachedCookies = Collections.unmodifiableMap(cookies);
		state = READ;
		return cachedCookies;
	}

pseudo_code:
```
// Function to get cached cookies
FUNCTION getCachedCookies() RETURNS Map<CharSequence, Set<Cookie>> 
    // Check if the state can be changed from NOT_READ to READING
    IF NOT STATE.compareAndSet(this, NOT_READ, READING) THEN 
        // Wait until the state is READ
        WHILE TRUE DO 
            IF state == READ THEN 
                RETURN cachedCookies
            END IF
        END WHILE
    END IF

    // Retrieve all cookie headers
    List<String> allCookieHeaders = nettyHeaders.getAll(cookiesHeaderName)
    // Initialize a map to store cookies
    Map<String, Set<Cookie>> cookies = new HashMap<>()

    // Process each cookie header
    FOR each aCookieHeader IN allCookieHeaders DO 
        // Variable to hold decoded cookies
        Set<Cookie> decode

        // Check if the channel is a client channel
        IF isClientChannel THEN 
            // Decode the cookie from the header
            Cookie c = ((ClientCookieDecoder) decoder).decode(aCookieHeader)
            // Retrieve existing cookies of the same name
            Set<Cookie> existingCookiesOfName = cookies.get(c.name())
            // If no existing cookies, initialize a new set
            IF existingCookiesOfName IS NULL THEN 
                existingCookiesOfName = new HashSet<>()
                cookies.put(c.name(), existingCookiesOfName)
            END IF
            // Add the cookie to the set
            existingCookiesOfName.add(c)
        ELSE 
            // Decode the cookies from the header for server channel
            decode = ((ServerCookieDecoder) decoder).decode(aCookieHeader)
            // Process each decoded cookie
            FOR each cookie IN decode DO 
                Set<Cookie> existingCookiesOfName = cookies.get(cookie.name())
                // If no existing cookies, initialize a new set
                IF existingCookiesOfName IS NULL THEN 
                    existingCookiesOfName = new HashSet<>()
                    cookies.put(cookie.name(), existingCookiesOfName)
                END IF
                // Add the cookie to the set
                existingCookiesOfName.add(cookie)
            END FOR
        END IF
    END FOR

    // Make the cached cookies map unmodifiable
    cachedCookies = Collections.unmodifiableMap(cookies)
    // Update the state to READ
    state = READ
    // Return the cached cookies
    RETURN cachedCookies
END FUNCTION
```

