docstring:
Parse a RES dataset from an input stream.
@param name the name of dataset.
@param stream the input stream of data.
@throws java.io.IOException

code:
public AttributeDataset parse(String name, InputStream stream) throws IOException, ParseException {
        BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(stream));

        String line = reader.readLine();
        if (line == null) {
            throw new IOException("Empty data source.");
        }

        String[] tokens = line.split("\t", -1);
        int p = (tokens.length - 2) / 2;

        line = reader.readLine();
        if (line == null) {
            throw new IOException("Premature end of file.");
        }

        String[] samples = line.split("\t", -1);
        if (samples.length != tokens.length-1) {
            throw new IOException("Invalid sample description header.");
        }

        Attribute[] attributes = new Attribute[p];
        for (int i = 0; i < p; i++) {
            attributes[i] = new NumericAttribute(tokens[2*i+2], samples[2*i+1]);
        }

        line = reader.readLine();
        if (line == null) {
            throw new IOException("Premature end of file.");
        }

        int n = Integer.parseInt(line);
        if (n <= 0) {
            throw new IOException("Invalid number of rows: " + n);            
        }

        AttributeDataset data = new AttributeDataset(name, attributes);

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            line = reader.readLine();
            if (line == null) {
                throw new IOException("Premature end of file.");
            }

            tokens = line.split("\t", -1);
            if (tokens.length != samples.length+1) {
                throw new IOException(String.format("Invalid number of elements of line %d: %d", i+4, tokens.length));
            }

            double[] x = new double[p];
            for (int j = 0; j < p; j++) {
                x[j] = Double.valueOf(tokens[2*j+2]);
            }

            AttributeDataset.Row datum = data.add(x);
            datum.name = tokens[1];
            datum.description = tokens[0];
        }

        reader.close();
        return data;
    }

pseudo_code:
```
// Function to parse a RES dataset from an input stream
FUNCTION parse(name: String, stream: InputStream) RETURNS AttributeDataset
    // Create a BufferedReader to read the input stream
    BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(stream))

    // Read the first line from the input stream
    String line = reader.readLine()
    // Check if the line is empty
    IF line IS NULL THEN
        THROW IOException("Empty data source.")

    // Split the first line into tokens based on tab delimiter
    String[] tokens = line.split("\t", -1)
    // Calculate the number of attributes
    int p = (tokens.length - 2) / 2

    // Read the second line from the input stream
    line = reader.readLine()
    // Check if the line is empty
    IF line IS NULL THEN
        THROW IOException("Premature end of file.")

    // Split the second line into sample descriptions
    String[] samples = line.split("\t", -1)
    // Validate the number of samples against tokens
    IF samples.length != tokens.length - 1 THEN
        THROW IOException("Invalid sample description header.")

    // Initialize an array of attributes
    Attribute[] attributes = new Attribute[p]
    // Create NumericAttribute objects for each attribute
    FOR i FROM 0 TO p - 1 DO
        attributes[i] = new NumericAttribute(tokens[2*i + 2], samples[2*i + 1])

    // Read the third line from the input stream
    line = reader.readLine()
    // Check if the line is empty
    IF line IS NULL THEN
        THROW IOException("Premature end of file.")

    // Parse the number of rows
    int n = Integer.parseInt(line)
    // Validate the number of rows
    IF n <= 0 THEN
        THROW IOException("Invalid number of rows: " + n)

    // Create an AttributeDataset with the name and attributes
    AttributeDataset data = new AttributeDataset(name, attributes)

    // Read data rows from the input stream
    FOR i FROM 0 TO n - 1 DO
        line = reader.readLine()
        // Check if the line is empty
        IF line IS NULL THEN
            THROW IOException("Premature end of file.")

        // Split the line into tokens
        tokens = line.split("\t", -1)
        // Validate the number of elements in the line
        IF tokens.length != samples.length + 1 THEN
            THROW IOException(String.format("Invalid number of elements of line %d: %d", i + 4, tokens.length))

        // Create an array to hold attribute values
        double[] x = new double[p]
        // Populate the attribute values
        FOR j FROM 0 TO p - 1 DO
            x[j] = Double.valueOf(tokens[2*j + 2])

        // Add a new row to the dataset
        AttributeDataset.Row datum = data.add(x)
        // Set the name and description for the row
        datum.name = tokens[1]
        datum.description = tokens[0]

    // Close the reader
    reader.close()
    // Return the populated dataset
    RETURN data
```

docstring:
Do the given block with the given service looked up.

This is invoked by {@link #doWithService(String, Descriptor.Call, Function)}, after wrapping the passed in block
in a circuit breaker if configured to do so.

The default implementation just delegates to the {@link #locate(String, Descriptor.Call)} method, but this method
can be overridden if the service locator wants to inject other behaviour after the service call is complete.

@param name The service name.
@param serviceCall The service call that needs the service lookup.
@param block A block of code that will use the looked up service, typically, to make a call on that service.
@return A future of the result of the block, if the service lookup was successful.

code:
protected <T> CompletionStage<Optional<T>> doWithServiceImpl(String name, Descriptor.Call<?, ?> serviceCall, Function<URI, CompletionStage<T>> block) {
        return locate(name, serviceCall).thenCompose(uri -> {
          return uri
                  .map(u -> block.apply(u).thenApply(Optional::of))
                  .orElseGet(() -> CompletableFuture.completedFuture(Optional.empty()));
        });
    }

pseudo_code:
```
// Pseudo-code for the doWithServiceImpl function

// FUNCTION declaration for handling service lookup and execution
FUNCTION doWithServiceImpl(name: String, serviceCall: Descriptor.Call<?, ?>, block: Function<URI, CompletionStage<T>>) RETURNS CompletionStage<Optional<T>>

    // Locate the service URI based on the service name and service call
    serviceUriFuture = locate(name, serviceCall) // Call the locate method to get the service URI

    // Chain the future to handle the result of the service URI lookup
    RETURN serviceUriFuture.thenCompose(uri -> // Process the result of the service URI lookup
        IF uri IS PRESENT THEN // Check if the URI is available
            // Apply the block to the URI and wrap the result in an Optional
            RETURN block.apply(uri).thenApply(Optional::of) // Execute the block with the URI and return the result wrapped in Optional
        ELSE
            // Return an empty Optional if no URI is found
            RETURN CompletableFuture.completedFuture(Optional.empty()) // Complete the future with an empty Optional
        END IF
    )

END FUNCTION
```

