docstring:
Compiles the TSQuery into an array of Query objects for execution.
If the user has not set a down sampler explicitly, and they don't want
millisecond resolution, then we set the down sampler to 1 second to handle
situations where storage may have multiple data points per second.
@param tsdb The tsdb to use for {@link TSDB#newQuery}
@return A deferred array of queries to wait on for compilation.
@since 2.2

code:
public Deferred<Query[]> buildQueriesAsync(final TSDB tsdb) {
    final Query[] tsdb_queries = new Query[queries.size()];

    final List<Deferred<Object>> deferreds =
        new ArrayList<Deferred<Object>>(queries.size());
    for (int i = 0; i < queries.size(); i++) {
      final Query query = tsdb.newQuery();
      deferreds.add(query.configureFromQuery(this, i));
      tsdb_queries[i] = query;
    }

    class GroupFinished implements Callback<Query[], ArrayList<Object>> {
      @Override
      public Query[] call(final ArrayList<Object> deferreds) {
        return tsdb_queries;
      }
      @Override
      public String toString() {
        return "Query compile group callback";
      }
    }

    return Deferred.group(deferreds).addCallback(new GroupFinished());
  }

pseudo_code:
```
// Function to build asynchronous queries for execution
FUNCTION buildQueriesAsync(tsdb: TSDB) RETURNS Deferred<Query[]>

    // Initialize an array to hold the compiled queries
    DECLARE tsdb_queries AS Array of Query WITH SIZE queries.size()

    // Initialize a list to hold deferred objects for the queries
    DECLARE deferreds AS List of Deferred<Object> WITH INITIAL CAPACITY queries.size()

    // Loop through each query in the queries list
    FOR i FROM 0 TO queries.size() - 1 DO
        // Create a new query object from the TSDB
        DECLARE query AS Query
        query = tsdb.newQuery()

        // Configure the query based on the current query and index
        deferreds.add(query.configureFromQuery(this, i))

        // Store the newly created query in the tsdb_queries array
        tsdb_queries[i] = query
    END FOR

    // Define a callback class for when the group of queries has finished
    CLASS GroupFinished IMPLEMENTS Callback<Query[], ArrayList<Object>>
        // Method called upon completion of the deferreds
        METHOD call(deferreds: ArrayList<Object>) RETURNS Query[]
            RETURN tsdb_queries
        END METHOD

        // Override the toString method for the callback
        METHOD toString() RETURNS String
            RETURN "Query compile group callback"
        END METHOD
    END CLASS

    // Group the deferreds and add a callback for when they finish
    RETURN Deferred.group(deferreds).addCallback(new GroupFinished())
END FUNCTION
```

