Sorts all array members into groups determined by the supplied mapping closure.
The closure should return the key that this item should be grouped by. The returned
LinkedHashMap will have an entry for each distinct key returned from the closure,
with each value being a list of items for that group.
<p>
Example usage:
<pre class="groovyTestCase">
Integer[] items = [1,2,3,4,5,6]
assert [0:[2,4,6], 1:[1,3,5]] == items.groupBy { it % 2 }
</pre>

@param self    an array to group
@param closure a closure mapping entries on keys
@return a new Map grouped by keys
@see #groupBy(Iterable, Closure)
@since 2.2.0

code:
public static <K, T> Map<K, List<T>> groupBy(T[] self, @ClosureParams(FirstParam.Component.class) Closure<K> closure) {
        return groupBy((Iterable<T>)Arrays.asList(self), closure);
    }

pseudo_code:
```
// Function to group array members based on a mapping closure
FUNCTION groupBy(self: Array, closure: Function) -> Map

    // Convert the input array to a list
    itemsList = Convert self to List

    // Initialize an empty Map to hold grouped items
    groupedMap = Create new Map

    // Iterate over each item in the itemsList
    FOR each item IN itemsList DO
        // Get the key from the closure for the current item
        key = closure(item)

        // Check if the key exists in the groupedMap
        IF key NOT IN groupedMap THEN
            // Initialize a new list for this key
            groupedMap[key] = Create new List

        // Add the current item to the list corresponding to the key
        groupedMap[key].ADD(item)

    END FOR

    // Return the grouped Map
    RETURN groupedMap
END FUNCTION
```

